HTML Maps
map : to create an html page different types of image map such as circle, rectangle, polygon etc.
as image map lets you make different clickable areas on an image which can be linked to different destinations.
in html this is done using the <map> and <area> tags.
2 types of links:
absolute and relative links.
    Basic tage used in HTML maps:
    <map> : This tag is used to define an image map. It contains one or more <area> tags.
    <area> : This tag is used to define a clickable area within an image map. Different shapes can be defined using the shape attribute (rect, circle, poly, default).
    <img> : This tag is used to embed an image in the HTML document and associate it with an image map using the usemap attribute.
basic syntax:
<img src="image.jpg" usemap="#mapname" >
<map name="mapname">
    <area shape="rect" coords="x1,y1,x2,y2" href="link1.html" alt="Description1">
    <area shape="circle" coords="x,y,radius" href="link2.html" alt="Description2">
</map>

shape : rect, circle, poly, default
coords : specifies the coordinates for the shape
href : page to open when the area is clicked
alt : alternative text for the area

image maps advantages:
1 to make images interactive
2 to reduce multiple images 
3 useful diagrams , geographycal maps , dashboards etc.m


rec coord takes 4 values x1,y1,x2,y2
circle coord takes 3 values x,y,radius
